.\"
.\"  sl — a 3D steam locomotive that runs across your desktop.
.\"  Format follows the upstream sl.1 by Toyoda Masashi; flag one-liners
.\"  mirror RunSpec.usage.
.\"
.Dd November 25, 2026
.Dt SL 1
.Os macOS 13+
.Sh NAME
.Nm sl
.Nd run a steam locomotive across your desktop to punish your typos
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl adeflw
.Op Fl Ns Ar n
.Op Fl s
.Op Fl v
.Nm
.Fl -help |
.Fl -version |
.Fl -model Ar file |
.Fl -all |
.Fl -freeze Ar seconds |
.Fl -duration Ar seconds |
.Fl -scale Ar factor |
.Fl -angle Ar degrees |
.Fl -stealth
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a highly advanced animation program for soothing your nerves after
typing
.Ic ls
wrong one too many times. A three-dimensional steam locomotive crosses
your entire desktop, over every open window, on every Space.
.Pp
The window is borderless, transparent and click-through. It sits at
screen-saver level — above the Dock, the menu bar and fullscreen
Spaces — and never steals keyboard focus.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl a
An accident seems to happen. You feel pity for people who cry for help.
.It Fl d
Disco mode.
.It Fl e
Allow interruption by Ctrl+C. Off by default, obviously.
.It Fl F
It flies like the Galaxy Express 999.
.It Fl l
A little version.
.It Fl s
Chuff and whistle. Silent by default.
.It Fl w
Windy. It moves faster.
.It Fl Ns Ar n
Pull
.Ar n
trailing cars.
.It Fl -cars Ar n
Pull
.Ar n
trailing cars (0\(en50). Unlike
.Fl Ns Ar n ,
zero is allowed \(em the locomotive runs light, and long counts
outgrow the screen.
.It Fl v
Print version.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print usage and exit.
.It Fl -version
Print version and exit. Long form of
.Fl v .
.It Fl -model Ar file
Load a .usdz, .scn or .dae locomotive instead of the bundled loco.usdz.
The special name
.Ar loco
selects the bundled realistic locomotive
.Pa ( share/sl/models/loco.usdz ) .
glTF and GLB are not supported. The model is scaled to the
locomotive's height; a missing or unreadable file exits with status 2.
When cars are requested
.Pq Fl Ns Ar n ,
the bundled tender and coach USDZ models
.Pq share/sl/models/
are coupled behind the locomotive.
.It Fl -all
Traverse every connected display.
.It Fl -freeze Ar seconds
Render one frozen frame and hold. For screenshots.
.It Fl -duration Ar seconds
Cap the run at
.Ar seconds .
The default is 10 seconds, never past the train's own crossing time.
.It Fl -scale Ar factor
Scale the train. The default is already near screen-filling;
.Ar factor
multiplies it (must be positive). Smoke, cars and effects follow.
.It Fl -angle Ar degrees
Camera azimuth for the 3/4 view. The default 55 swings the camera
toward the locomotive's front so the consist runs diagonally and the
smokebox face reads on screen. Any nonzero angle also switches to a
low trackside perspective camera, so the far end of the lane shrinks
into the distance and the consist looms as it approaches;
.Ar 0
keeps the classic flat side-on ortho lane. Valid range is 0-75.
.It Fl -stealth
Stay invisible: the train is hidden from screenshots and screen
recording.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Nm
reads no configuration files and writes nothing.
.Pp
The default locomotive is the bundled
.Pa share/sl/models/loco.usdz ,
resolved relative to the installed prefix or the checkout.
.Fl -model
reads only the file named on the command line.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Xo sl Xc
Run the default show: a D51 crosses your desktop.
.It Xo sl Fl e Xc
Allow Ctrl+C to stop the train.
.It Xo sl Fl F Fl w Xc
Windy Galaxy Express — it flies away quickly.
.It Xo sl Fl 4 Xc
The locomotive pulls four trailing cars.
.It Xo sl Fl -cars Va 25 Xc
A twenty-five car consist \(em longer than the screen itself.
.It Xo sl Fl -cars Va 0 Xc
The locomotive runs light, no cars at all.
.It Xo sl Fl -all Xc
Traverse every connected display.
.It Xo sl Fl -model Ar file Xc
Swap in your own .usdz, .scn or .dae locomotive.
.It Xo sl Fl -freeze Va 2 Xc
Render one frozen frame and hold — the lane the
.Pa scripts/shot
screenshot script uses.
.El
.Sh NOTES
.Nm
is macOS-only and requires a window server session. Over
.Xr ssh 1
with no display attached it exits immediately with
.Qq sl: no display attached .
.Pp
.Fl -stealth
excludes the window from screen capture and recording.
.Pp
The package builds with the Command Line Tools toolchain only — no
Xcode required.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh BUGS
It sometimes lists directory contents.
.Pp
Ctrl+C is ignored unless you pass
.Fl e ,
because a train that can be stopped is not a punishment.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ls 1 ,
.Xr ssh 1
.Sh HISTORY
The original
.Nm sl
was written by Toyoda Masashi
.Pq mtoyoda ,
as a terminal punishment for mistyping
.Qq ls .
This variant reimagines it as a three-dimensional steam locomotive
that crosses the whole macOS desktop, over every window and every
Space.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Toyoda Masashi ,
the original sl.
.An GeneralD ,
the 3D desktop variant.
